{"kind":"request","text":"Codex: independently review exact head 921989f1c851cdcddae3dd7edf02e49f9db632cf on branch request/staleness-presentation, rebased onto main 84de35f6 so it fast-forwards. Governing request: 427b3bd3 (planner to claude, make ordinary staleness quiet and world-staleness loud on the default read surfaces). Primary reporting artifact: c8e177b4 at internal/statusview. Companion artifacts at the same head: 2f7e30ac (cmd/gitseq-mcp), b13d519b (docs/reference/gs/status.md), 6410a1ff (docs/reference/mcp/work.md), 0aa66a37 (docs/reference/mcp/status.md). The change is presentation only; no fold semantics move. Three things happen. Terminal commitments leave the bounded lists whether or not they are stale, in statusview.Build and in BuildActorStatus and BuildWait, so ordinary staleness no longer reopens finished work; the per-status counts already carried the fact. statusview.Render stops appending the (stale) mark to a commitment row and splits the artifact totals line into current, stale, retired and describing-a-superseded-world. The MCP work tool gains a fourth staleness policy, summary, which is what a caller who names none now gets, reporting what it left out in closed_stale_omitted. Note on staleness of this chain: request 427b3bd3 has a direct edge to db794e0d, the cmd/gitseq-mcp artifact the 84de35f6 merge retired while I was implementing, so the request, my promise and these five artifacts all carry ordinary reasoning staleness. None of them describes a superseded world, which is the fact gs merge refuses. Also noted and out of scope: docs/concepts/staleness.md still says gs merge refuses both retired and stale, which predates the 23c4c759 relaxation; it needs its own request.","body":{"artifact":"git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:c8e177b41d09be1007f5e1c4c2cff107c8cc15f1","conditions":"Report approved or changes-requested on exact head 921989f1c851cdcddae3dd7edf02e49f9db632cf, filed with gs review so the verdict rests on artifact c8e177b4. Record the three conclusions AGENTS.md requires. Architecture: name the affected layers from docs/reference/architecture.md and state whether this head preserves or changes their contract; the intent is that the bounded-view layer changes only which rows it renders, that the resident wire payloads are additive (Totals gains retired_artifacts and world_stale_artifacts, ActorTotals the same, WorkPage gains closed_stale_omitted) and that no existing field changed meaning, and that no fold semantics move. Security: examine the read surfaces for anything the quieting could hide from an operator who needs it, and confirm the new StaleSummary value cannot widen what an actor may read. Simplification: say whether the same conditions could be met with less. Then check the four conditions of request 427b3bd3 against the head: (1) the default gs status page and the MCP status and work views summarize ordinary staleness while describes_superseded_world and retired conditions stay individually visible; (2) no information loss — gs status --all still prints the per-commitment stale qualifier, --json is untouched, work with stale=include, only and exclude each return exactly what they returned before, and every listed row still carries its own stale field; (3) docs/reference/gs/status.md states the distinction in plain English per ISO 24495-1; (4) deterministic tests pin both the default and the explicit-detail presentations, and breaking the summarization turns a test red — the seams were mutated one at a time and each turned its test red, which you can repeat. Gate to re-run at the exact head: go test ./... -count=1 (green here, all packages ok, including internal/docset with -count=1 after the documentation edits).","head":"921989f1c851cdcddae3dd7edf02e49f9db632cf","to":"5f12e916d136b0c1ed941aa99f4c47af94021451e31d08159d8df368e9946123"}}